        "pre_narrative": "The Overwrought Orator has the opposite problem: he is tasked with writing accessible safety instructions for palace servants, but everything he writes sounds like a coronation speech. His fire evacuation notice begins: \"Whereas, in the event that conflagration should beset these hallowed halls...\" The servants cannot follow it.",
        "passage": "Fire safety is everyone's responsibility. If you see smoke or flames, leave the building immediately using the nearest staircase. Do not use the service elevators. [1] Pursuant to the aforementioned protocols of egress and in accordance with established emergency procedure, the designated muster point for all personnel is the east courtyard.",
        "question_stem": "Which choice best replaces the underlined sentence [1] to match the clear, accessible register of the passage?",
