        "enemy_type": "Palace Courtier",
        "pre_narrative": "The Imperial Scribe is writing a formal history of the Keep's founding for the royal library. The first half of each paragraph is excellent. Then something goes wrong. His description of the first Keep's construction reads like a chronicle, and then suddenly reads like he's texting a friend. You must restore consistency.",
        "passage": "The founding of the Keep marked a pivotal moment in the region's history. Under the direction of High Architect Maren, construction began in the spring of the first reign year, drawing on labor and materials from seven allied territories. The project required coordination of unprecedented scale, involving thousands of workers and the transport of stone across three mountain passes. [1] The high walls rose in sections, each fitted with the precise interlocking stonework for which Keep architecture became renowned throughout the known world. [2] tbh the sheer scale of it was insane and it's honestly impressive anyone pulled it off.",
