        "enemy_name": "The Vague Valuer",
        "enemy_type": "Palace Courtier",
        "pre_narrative": "The Vague Valuer is the palace's official appraiser. He assesses the value of everything in the Keep and describes it as \"good,\" \"nice,\" \"pretty good,\" or, when pressed, \"very good.\" His appraisal reports are useless for insurance purposes. You must introduce him to the concept of precision.",
        "passage": "The Keep's new grain storage system has performed well since its installation last spring. The sealed chambers have proven to be particularly good at preventing the moisture damage that destroyed much of the harvest two years ago.",
        "question_stem": "Which word or phrase most precisely and effectively replaces the underlined word \"good\" in the passage?",
