        "pre_narrative": "You enter the throne room of the Redundancy King. Every wall bears the same tapestry. Every column is doubled. The King speaks: \"Welcome, welcome. I have been expecting you, and I also anticipated your arrival.\" He gestures to a scroll. The first battle begins.",
        "passage": "Scholars who study ancient languages, [A] which are languages that are no longer spoken by any living population, often work in isolation. The field requires patience and a tolerance for ambiguity that most researchers find challenging.",
        "question_stem": "The writer is considering the underlined clause [A]: \"which are languages that are no longer spoken by any living population.\" Should this clause be kept or deleted?",
