        "pre_narrative": "The King has written a sentence about a battle. In it, the battle is described as having studied battle plans before dawn, and a decision is described as being made by the smell of smoke. Both problems are in the same sentence. This is the modifier question from which lesser grammarians do not return.",
        "passage": null,
        "question_stem": "Which version of the following sentence correctly places all modifiers?\n\nHaving reviewed the battle plans before dawn, the decision to advance was made by the commander based only on the initial reports.",
        "option_a": "Having reviewed the battle plans before dawn, the decision to advance was made by the commander based only on the initial reports.",
